RetroBoot: nubus-qfb takes 32 in its depth register as millions, as at realize (m68k series).

The qfb driver's open (ClassicMac qfb/driver main.cc) writes 32 to the depth
register when the card starts in millions (slot PRAM mode $85, nubus-qfb
depth=24 or 32); its cscSetMode/cscSwitchMode write 24.  QEMU accepted only
1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and 24 and took 32 as 1 bit, so a Mac that starts in millions
drew 32-bit pixels into a 1-bit screen (lab: Mac OS 8.1, seed mode $85).
Realize already maps a depth property of 32 to 24; the register now does too.

diff --git a/hw/display/mac_qfb.c b/hw/display/mac_qfb.c
index e58fda54bb..1f1ff35ca6 100644
--- a/hw/display/mac_qfb.c
+++ b/hw/display/mac_qfb.c
@@ -529,6 +529,14 @@ static void qfb_ctrl_write(void *opaque,
         case 1: case 2: case 4: case 8: case 16: case 24:
             s->depth = val;
             break;
+        case 32:
+            /*
+             * RetroBoot: millions, as at realize.  The driver's open writes
+             * 32 when the card starts in millions (cscSetMode writes 24);
+             * taken as 1 bit, Mac OS drew 32-bit pixels into a 1-bit screen.
+             */
+            s->depth = 24;
+            break;
         default:
             s->depth = 1;
             break;
